Library/
Temp/
Logs/
obj/
UserSettings/
Builds/
*.csproj
*.sln
.vs/

# Left by com.unity.test-framework.performance when a build fails or is refused at preprocess.
# PingCore.Editor.Cli.BuildHousekeeping removes them, and the empty folder with its .meta, after every
# ClientBuild and BuildServer run; these lines are only a backstop for an editor killed
# mid-build. SampleGame has no Resources folder of its own; if it ever gets one, drop the last line.
Assets/Resources/PerformanceTestRun*
Assets/Resources/PerformanceTestRun*.meta
Assets/Resources.meta

# Written by the Package Manager window with nothing but Unity's defaults (the main registry, no scoped
# registry). SampleGame needs no scoped registry; if it ever does, commit this file instead.
ProjectSettings/PackageManagerSettings.asset

# never import the Quickstart into SampleGame (GUID collisions): it is a generated copy of Beacon Rush with the
# same GUIDs and assembly names. These lines keep a stray import out of git.
Assets/Samples/
Assets/Samples.meta
